From: nuubOS Project
Subject: [PATCH] Input: adc-joystick: use ABS code when inverting axes

adc-joystick stores the EV_ABS code associated with each ADC channel, but
passes the channel index to adc_joystick_invert().

This only works accidentally while the channel index matches the EV_ABS
code. For a four-axis joystick using ABS_X, ABS_Y, ABS_RX and ABS_RY, the
third channel has index 2 while its input code is ABS_RX (3). The driver
therefore reads the min/max parameters for ABS_Z and can generate invalid
negative values when the axis is inverted.

Use the configured EV_ABS code for the axis when looking up its range.

Signed-off-by: nuubOS Project
---
 drivers/input/joystick/adc-joystick.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/input/joystick/adc-joystick.c b/drivers/input/joystick/adc-joystick.c
--- a/drivers/input/joystick/adc-joystick.c
+++ b/drivers/input/joystick/adc-joystick.c
@@ -45,7 +45,7 @@ static void adc_joystick_poll(struct input_dev *input)
 		if (ret < 0)
 			return;
 		if (joy->axes[i].inverted)
-			val = adc_joystick_invert(input, i, val);
+			val = adc_joystick_invert(input, joy->axes[i].code, val);
 		input_report_abs(input, joy->axes[i].code, val);
 	}
 	input_sync(input);
@@ -95,7 +95,7 @@ static int adc_joystick_handle(const void *data, void *private)
 		else
 			val &= GENMASK(msb, 0);
 		if (joy->axes[i].inverted)
-			val = adc_joystick_invert(joy->input, i, val);
+			val = adc_joystick_invert(joy->input, joy->axes[i].code, val);
 		input_report_abs(joy->input, joy->axes[i].code, val);
 	}

